                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "584a8733-9b43-3eff-8eb6-1aaa211c3b30",
                        "entry_id": "18818d1e-4735-3090-ac78-e3823a16dbf2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Partie de la philosophie morale qui traite des expériences de pensée impliquant un tramway."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Par plaisanterie",
                            "Extrêmement rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebdc5ae5-5974-4084-8780-dc27e0909915",
                                "sense_id": "584a8733-9b43-3eff-8eb6-1aaa211c3b30",
                                "text": "Ainsi, le cas du Tramway qui tue a engendré une incroyable prolifération de variantes parfois complètement baroques. Il a suscité une énorme quantité de travaux et de débats (des millions d’entrées sur le Net), parfois si sophistiqués que seuls quelques initiés peuvent encore les suivre. On en est au point où l’on peut dire ironiquement, mais avec une pointe de vérité quand même, qu’une nouvelle discipline scientifique est née : la tramwayologie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36343b09-fc4f-45bc-bde6-d74852fcb638",
                        "source_entry_id": "18818d1e-4735-3090-ac78-e3823a16dbf2",
                        "source_sense_id": "584a8733-9b43-3eff-8eb6-1aaa211c3b30",
                        "target_lang_word": "trolleyology",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trolleyology",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "276f30dd-10f3-326c-afd1-e5bd95f12a5c",
                                        "entry_id": "6e0760ad-3262-37f0-8b56-5d09a98f86e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An area of philosophy dealing with the kind of moral dilemma typified by the trolley problem of whether to sacrifice one person to save others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "humorous",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06df264c-b41d-46f3-a333-c38ccf922f3e",
                                                "sense_id": "276f30dd-10f3-326c-afd1-e5bd95f12a5c",
                                                "text": "Trolleyology . . . by now the philosophical commentary on these cases makes the Talmud look like Cliffs Notes, and is surely massive enough to stop any runaway trolley in its tracks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c551e2f2-f509-44c5-9075-8c4948fef132",
                                                "sense_id": "276f30dd-10f3-326c-afd1-e5bd95f12a5c",
                                                "text": "It used to be that the only people who had even heard of such dilemmas were professional philosophers, but now it seems as if everyone is doing trolleyology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c6077ae-2076-4fe4-8e73-f8832e1d37be",
                                                "sense_id": "276f30dd-10f3-326c-afd1-e5bd95f12a5c",
                                                "text": "Patients with damage to this area are overwhelmingly utilitarian in their moral judgments in the case studies presented to them – trolleyology and many others."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
